ted_at":"2025-12-14T15:12:06.150Z","voted_up":true,"votes_funny":"1","votes_up":"0","written_during_early_access":false},{"rec_id":"32571109","appid":"375460","author_id":"76561198093355799","language":"english","last_played":"1620854376","num_reviews":"340","playtime_at_review":"358","playtime_forever":"382","received_for_free":false,"review":"16bit Trader is a mobile, medieval, strategy, management trading game, where you try to become the richest trader in the entire land.\nThe point of the game is to buy cheap items in one location and sell it for a higher price in a different location. \nSounds easy right?! Well it isn't!\n\nWhenever I buy items the price for that item immediately drops in all the cities I visit. \nAs soon as I sell it, it goes up.\nYou can do quests, but you need to travel to places!\nTraveling cost money and often you come across some bandits that steal your money and loot.\nYou also spend way more gold traveling to those locations than you get as reward at the end of the quest.\n\nI started to doubt myself... Was this game really that hard? or am i just not playing it right?\nThe game tells you to learn the prices so you can use it to your advantage. \nI soon noticed that wouldn't matter because the prices are random!\nWhen you leave a city and come back the store prices change at random which makes learning the prices and using them to your advantage impossible.\nI always had to sell my items at a loss because I had run out of gold and couldn't travel any further.\nWhen you are out of money it's just game over!\nKeeping your money or buying items won't make a difference because you loose your money to thief's and traveling anyways. \n\nThe only positive thing I can possibly say about this game is that i enjoyed the music, The fact that it has trading cards and that i enjoyed the art style. \nBut don't let the nice cartoonie (not even 16bit) looking game fool you.\nThe game is no fun and not worth 2,99€!","sent_compound":0.8517000079154968,"sentiment_0_10":9.258500099182129,"sentiment_0_10_round":9,"updated_at":"2025-12-14T15:12:03.849Z","voted_up":false,"votes_funny":"0","votes_up":"16","written_during_early_access":false},{"rec_id":"21201969","appid":"375460","author_id":"76561198161027732","language":"english","last_played":"1457113745","num_reviews":"1","playtime_at_review":"71","playtime_forever":"128","received_for_free":false,"review":"To be fair, I enjoyed this game when I first started playing it. It looked pretty cute, nothing groundbreaking, but better than average mobile game style graphics that suggested some care and consideration had gone into it. The translation isn't as bad as others have said - yes the English is a bit wrong in places but hardly enough to trip you up. The only problem I had with the game at first was that the economic mechanics weren't great. When the price of one commodity went up, they all went up, and usually by similar amounts, so the trading side of the game lacked a bit of depth and nuance. And since that's the sole focus of the game, it does make it feel a bit basic.\n\nHowever, what really broke this game for me was the save function not working or being unreliable. After playing for an hour, saving fairly regularly in the first save slot and then saving and quitting, I found that the game had only saved my progress sporadically. So when I went back to it, I had essentially lost about 20 minutes of progress. I played for a while longer, saving and quitting and reloading to see if there was any fix or if it was a one time glitch, but no. This game will not let you save. That's the bottom line. And for a relatively shallow game to have so major a glitch, is a deal breaker for me. I only paid 33p for it, so I'll let it run to get the cards, but otherwise, it's not worth your time.","sent_compound":0.9685999751091003,"sentiment_0_10":9.843000411987305,"sentiment_0_10_round":10,"updated_at":"2025-12-14T15:12:05.247Z","voted_up":false,"votes_funny":"0","votes_up":"0